# Code Conventions

- **TypeScript strict mode everywhere.** No `any`, no `as unknown as` casts to silence the compiler. If a type is hard to express, ask before bypassing the type system.
- **Shared types live in `packages/types`** (`@acc/types`) and are imported by both `apps/api` and `apps/mobile`. Never duplicate enums, constants, DTOs, or schemas across the apps.
- **No business logic in controllers.** NestJS controllers only handle routing/request-response wiring; all business logic goes in services. Keep modules feature-scoped.
- **All datetimes are stored in UTC** (spec §23). Transmit as ISO 8601 strings; format to the ground's local timezone only at display time on mobile. Aggregations and the 5-hour scorecard window are computed in UTC.
- **Online-only. Offline scoring is OUT of scope** (spec §12.4, §30.2). Do not add offline queues, local write-then-sync layers, optimistic offline mutation caches, or any "works without network" scoring path.
- Money/fees are stored in cents as BIGINT — never floats.
- Derived cricket stats (averages, strike rate, economy) are computed at query time, never persisted denormalized.
- all text inputs use the shared TextInput wrapper, which carries the white fill, 8px radius (`rounded-control` via `fieldStyles`), soft shadow, and label styling, so screens should pass a label prop rather than styling fields inline. Buttons use the shared Button wrapper with the same `rounded-control` token — do not set radius on inputs or buttons inline.
- form field labels use the shared input components' default brown style (font-sans text-base leading-6 text-[#5A4136]), so screens shouldn't set label colors inline. 
- form fields show validation via the shared TextInput error prop (red text below + red border), not custom per-screen error UI.
- **Destructive confirmations (mobile):** use `confirmDestructiveDeleteAlert` from `apps/mobile/src/lib/confirm-destructive-delete.ts` for all delete/permanent-remove actions. It renders the native iOS/Android alert (neutral Cancel + red Delete). Do not build custom Modal confirmation dialogs for deletes. On API failure, show a follow-up `Alert.alert` with the error message (same pattern as Delete User / Delete Tournament).
- **Mobile screen headers:** every stack screen uses `ScreenHeader` from `apps/mobile/src/components/ui/ScreenHeader.tsx` (orange circular back arrow left, optional title/subtitle, `ProfileMenu` avatar right). Tab/dashboard roots use `DashboardHeader` (greeting + profile menu, no back arrow). **Exception:** the live ball-by-ball scoring screen (`matches/[matchId]/score.tsx`) keeps its dedicated compact header. Auth/onboarding screens (login, signup, OTP, password reset) omit `ProfileMenu` and may use `showBack` only. Do not add bespoke `← Back` text links or one-off header rows.
- **Mobile keyboard-aware forms:** every screen with text inputs uses `KeyboardAwareFormScrollView` from `apps/mobile/src/components/ui/KeyboardAwareFormScrollView.tsx` as the scroll container (not raw `ScrollView` + ad-hoc `KeyboardAvoidingView`). Keep fixed headers and bottom action bars **outside** the scroll view; pass sticky footers via the `footer` prop when they must stay above the keyboard. List screens with a search field + `FlatList` use `KeyboardAwareFormContainer` instead. Modals/sheets with inputs use `KeyboardAwareFormScrollView` with `compact`. The shared `TextInput` auto-scrolls on focus when inside these wrappers.
